  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Nagnath S/O. Haribhau Munde vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 January, 2020 Author: R. G. Avachat Bench: R. G. Avachat 1 aba-1512-19.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1512 Of 2019 Nagnath Haribhau Munde ... Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent .... Mr. N. D. Kendre, Advocate for applicant. Mr. V. S. Badakh, App for respondent-State. .... Coram : R. G. Avachat, J. Dated : 06th January, 2020 Per Court :- . This is an application for bail under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure. The applicant claims to have an apprehension of being arrested in connection with Crime No.0162/2019 registered at Tadaklas Police Station, Taluka Purna, District Parbhani, for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 328, 272, 273, read with Section 34 of Indian Penal Code and under Section 26(2) (Iv), 27(3) (D), 27(3) (E), 30(2) (a) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, Nagnath S/O. Haribhau Munde vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 January, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/128578600/ 1 2006. 1 of 3 ::: Uploaded on - 08/01/2020 ::: Downloaded on - 08/01/2020 23:48:01 : 2 aba-1512-19.doc 2.",
    "facts": "Perused the First Information Report (FIR) and related papers. Except the offence under Section 328 of Indian Penal Code, rest of the offences are bailable one. I am of the view that Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code, may not be applicable to the present case. The crime came to be registered against the applicant simply because of seizure of the Gutkha in the truck. He was called by the truck driver. The articles came to be seized from the truck. The applicant is neither the truck driver nor owner of the truck. Prima-facie, there is nothing to connect the applicant with the crime in question.",
